From 53d82ffb795046d1ba50b552e311cac2bd4c7164 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:04:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] CUDA/HIP: one element-wise kernel for Inkling 2's SITU
 expert activation

situ(g, u) = (tanh(g/beta)*beta * sigmoid(g)) * (tanh(u/lb)*lb) ran as four
kernels after every gate_up product (softcap, sigmoid*mul, softcap, mul),
each reading and writing the 8 x 1152 activations of a token. The nine nodes
now match as one kernel that reads g and u straight from the two strided
halves of the gate_up output. It uses the expressions of the kernels it
replaces, in their order, so the output is bit-identical, for one token and
for prompt batches alike.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL: 1,876 -> 1,732 kernels per generated token;
tg128 56.1 -> 57.3 tok/s (+2.1%). KLD against the previous commit,
wiki.test.raw -c 512, -ub 512 and -ub 1: 0. New test-backend-ops case SITU
(one token, a 37-token batch, an odd shape).
